{
  "dom_id": "step-q183924",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Consider the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+8,\\,{a}_{1}=4,\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nSuppose we wish to prove the following statement using mathematical induction:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=4(2n-1)\n$$\n\nA proof template is outlined below. Fill in the missing statements.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case $n=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & ={{field-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n=$ {{field-2}}, we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{k}={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{a}_{k+1}={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, ${a}_{n}=4(2n-1)$ for all $n\\in N.$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
